{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And when you slaughter.</b> He explained that when He said, “I am YHWH your Elohim” (Exodus 20:2) — that they should accept Him alone as their Elohim, just as they accepted Him at the Exodus, saying, “This is my El and I will beautify Him, the El of my father and I will exalt Him” (Exodus 15:2) — He not only said that they should keep His commandments and exalt Him as is fitting for one who has accepted a king, and that they should pray to Him alone in all their troubles, but along with this He warned them to be greatly zealous for His honor, so that they do not profane His holy things even in thought."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:51.854361632Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}